Day 21 of the Claude Coding Challenge: Building a Digital Footprint Analyzer

Today’s challenge explores something most of us rarely see—the hidden connections behind our digital lives.

Using Claude, I built a Digital Footprint Analyzer that reveals how our online data is interconnected across the apps and platforms we use every day. Simply provide up to 15 frequently used apps, and the system automatically traces them back to their parent companies, uncovering how data flows through the digital ecosystem.

🔍 The analyzer generates a comprehensive dashboard in seconds, featuring:

✅ Digital Footprint Overview
✅ Digital Twin Profile
✅ Exposure Heat Map
✅ Parent Company Rankings
✅ Data Collection Metrics
✅ Privacy Risk Radar
✅ Surprising Insights & Hidden Connections
✅ Most Valuable Data Points Being Collected

What makes this exercise fascinating is seeing how seemingly unrelated apps are often owned by the same organizations, creating a much larger digital footprint than most people realize.

This project demonstrates the power of AI not only to build applications rapidly but also to help individuals better understand their privacy exposure and digital identity.

As AI continues to accelerate software development, tools like this make complex data analysis accessible to everyone—turning what would normally take hours of research into a few seconds of automated insight.

Try it yourself and discover:
👉 Which companies know the most about you
👉 How your data travels across platforms
👉 Where your biggest privacy risks may exist

The results may surprise you.

